' LibraryStore — saved content and continue-watching positions, persisted
' locally, pure logic on a registry seam like SettingsStore/AddonsStore.
'
' A real store is built over an roRegistrySection and Load()s its state on
' construction; tests pass a fake registry (or nothing, which means in-memory
' only). Save() writes the whole library as one registry key. Since the app is
' guest-only nothing syncs — this is the local mirror of the Stremio library.
'
' Persistence is a session-aware registry key: a guest session uses "library"
' and a stremio session uses "stremio_library", so the two sessions never share
' saved content or continue-watching positions. What persists differs by
' session: a guest session saves saved items + continue watching (its data is
' local-only, nothing to fetch anywhere), while a stremio session persists ONLY
' the continue-watching stack — the rest of its library is re-synced from the
' Stremio account in the background on launch and lives in memory for the
' session, so nothing is written to the device needlessly. The registry section
' object is shared; only the key changes.
'
' Ordering is the array itself: freshly written items land at index 0, so the
' newest is always first and no sequence number or sort is needed. Continue
' watching is a capped stack — SetPosition drops the old entry for the same
' video/series, pushes the new one on top, and pops anything beyond the cap.
'
' Helpers live as instance methods: Roku scopes user-defined global functions
' per component, so a bare global called from a method that is invoked from
' another component's code would resolve to invalid (call of a non-function).
'
' Watched state is two layers merged at read time:
'   - the local set (m.watched) is display-side only, written by
'     MarkWatchedIfFinished / MarkSeriesDone, persisted with the saved items so
'     it survives reloads. It is never pushed to the account.
'   - the account layer (m.accountWatched) is re-derived on every sync from the
'     libraryItem state (watched bitfield, flaggedWatched/timesWatched flags,
'     timeOffset), memory-only for the session.
' Internally watched is keyed by videoId (a movie's metaId, or a series'
' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}") so grid tiles ask coarsely with a metaId while
' EpisodesScreen asks per episode.

' Guest libraries persist to the device registry, whose size budget is real, so
' the guest saved list is capped: adding beyond MAX_GUEST_SAVED evicts the
' oldest entry (the array is newest-first, so the tail is least recent),
' mirroring the continue-watching cap. A stremio session is memory-only — its
' saved map is re-synced from the account every launch — so it is never capped
' and the account stays the authority on how many items it holds.
const MAX_GUEST_SAVED = 100

' A video counts as watched when the player position has reached ~70% of its
' duration (so a movie/episode finished per Stremio's rule). position/duration
' are milliseconds; the comparison stays on integer math.
const WATCHED_THRESHOLD = 0.7
const MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING = 8

class LibraryStore
    registry as dynamic
    sessionType as string
    saved as object
    savedOrder as object
    positions as object
    stremioLibrary as object
    watched as object
    accountWatched as object

    sub new(registry = invalid as dynamic, sessionType = "guest" as string)
        m.registry = registry
        m.sessionType = "guest"
        if sessionType = "stremio" then m.sessionType = "stremio"
        m.saved = {}
        m.savedOrder = []
        m.positions = []
        m.stremioLibrary = []
        m.watched = {}
        m.accountWatched = {}
        m.Load()
    end sub

    ' A missing AA key reads back as invalid in BrightScript, so this stands in
    ' for roAssociativeArray.DidExist (which the brs interpreter does not
    ' implement).
    function HasKey(aa as object, key as string) as boolean
        if aa = invalid then return false
        return aa[key] <> invalid
    end function

    ' Add a series/movie to the saved library. False when already saved or the
    ' id is blank. A guest library is capped at MAX_GUEST_SAVED — adding past
    ' it drops the oldest entry so the device registry never overflows, exactly
    ' how the continue-watching stack is capped. A stremio session never caps:
    ' its saved map is memory-only and re-synced from the account, so the device
    ' budget does not apply there.
    function AddSaved(metaId as string, metaType as string, name as string, poster = "" as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" then return false
        if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId) then return false
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            while m.savedOrder.Count() >= MAX_GUEST_SAVED
                oldestId = m.savedOrder.Pop()
                m.saved.Delete(oldestId)
            end while
        end if
        m.saved[metaId] = {
            metaId: metaId
            metaType: metaType
            name: name
            poster: poster
        }
        m.savedOrder.Unshift(metaId)
        m.Save()
        return true
    end function

    function RemoveSaved(metaId as string) as boolean
        if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId)
            m.saved.Delete(metaId)
            for i = m.savedOrder.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
                if m.savedOrder[i] = metaId then m.savedOrder.Delete(i)
            end for
            m.Save()
            return true
        end if
        return false
    end function

    function IsSaved(metaId as string) as boolean
        return m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId)
    end function

    ' Most recently added first — the array holds ids newest-first.
    function SavedItems() as object
        items = []
        for each metaId in m.savedOrder
            if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId) then items.Push(m.saved[metaId])
        end for
        return items
    end function

    ' The saved list as the Library screen presents it: filtered by content type
    ' and ordered by one of the supported sorts, always a fresh array (the
    ' internal saved map/order are never rearranged — SortByName/SortByWatched
    ' only reorder the returned copy). typeFilter is "all", "movie" or "series";
    ' sort is "recent" (saved order, newest first — the default), "az"/"za"
    ' (case-insensitive by name) or "watched" (any saved item with a
    ' continue-watching position first, most recently watched first — the
    ' positions array is newest-first — then everything else by name).
    function LibraryView(typeFilter as string, sort as string) as object
        items = m.SavedItems()
        if typeFilter <> "all"
            filtered = []
            for each item in items
                metaType = item.metaType
                if metaType = invalid then metaType = ""
                if metaType = typeFilter then filtered.Push(item)
            end for
            items = filtered
        end if
        if sort = "az"
            m.SortByName(items, false)
        else if sort = "za"
            m.SortByName(items, true)
        else if sort = "watched"
            m.SortByWatched(items)
        end if
        return items
    end function

    ' Case-insensitive insertion sort of saved records by name, ascending or
    ' descending. An insertion sort keeps it interpreter-safe, exactly like
    ' SortByMtimeDesc; roArray.Sort with a function comparator is not guaranteed
    ' in the brs interpreter. A malformed (invalid/blank) name is coerced to ""
    ' so the compare cannot throw.
    sub SortByName(items as object, descending as boolean)
        for i = 1 to items.Count() - 1
            temp = items[i]
            j = i
            while j > 0
                left = items[j - 1].name
                if left = invalid then left = ""
                right = temp.name
                if right = invalid then right = ""
                if descending
                    if LCase(left) >= LCase(right) then exit while
                else
                    if LCase(left) <= LCase(right) then exit while
                end if
                items[j] = items[j - 1]
                j = j - 1
            end while
            items[j] = temp
        end for
    end sub

    ' Insertion sort that floats items with a continue-watching position to the
    ' front, most recently watched first (positions is newest-first, so the
    ' earliest array index is the freshest), then the unwatched by name. Any
    ' position under a metaId marks it watched — an episode position counts for
    ' its series.
    sub SortByWatched(items as object)
        rank = {}
        for i = 0 to m.positions.Count() - 1
            mid = m.positions[i].metaId
            if mid <> invalid and mid <> "" and not m.HasKey(rank, mid) then rank[mid] = i
        end for
        for i = 1 to items.Count() - 1
            temp = items[i]
            j = i
            while j > 0
                if not m.WatchedBefore(items[j - 1], temp, rank) then exit while
                items[j] = items[j - 1]
                j = j - 1
            end while
            items[j] = temp
        end for
    end sub

    ' true when a should sort after b in the "watched" sort: a is less recently
    ' watched (higher rank) than b, or equally ranked and names after b. Not
    ' ranked items all share the cap rank, so unwatched sort by name.
    function WatchedBefore(a as object, b as object, rank as object) as boolean
        ra = m.WatchedRank(rank, a.metaId)
        rb = m.WatchedRank(rank, b.metaId)
        if ra <> rb then return ra > rb
        an = a.name
        if an = invalid then an = ""
        bn = b.name
        if bn = invalid then bn = ""
        return LCase(an) > LCase(bn)
    end function

    function WatchedRank(rank as object, metaId as string) as integer
        if metaId <> invalid and metaId <> "" and m.HasKey(rank, metaId) then return rank[metaId]
        return 1000000000
    end function

    ' Record playback progress for a video (a movie metaId, or the
    ' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}" id for an episode). Drops the previous
    ' entry for the same video or series, pushes the new one on top of the
    ' capped stack, and pops anything beyond MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING. Blank
    ' positions are ignored so a fresh screen never clears stored progress.
    sub SetPosition(videoId as string, metaId as string, metaType as string, season as integer, episode as integer, name as string, poster = "" as string, position = 0 as integer, duration = 0 as integer)
        if videoId = "" or metaId = "" then return
        for i = m.positions.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            if m.positions[i].videoId = videoId or m.positions[i].metaId = metaId
                m.positions.Delete(i)
            end if
        end for
        m.positions.Unshift({
            videoId: videoId
            metaId: metaId
            metaType: metaType
            season: season
            episode: episode
            name: name
            poster: poster
            position: position
            duration: duration
        })
        while m.positions.Count() > MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING
            m.positions.Pop()
        end while
        m.Save()
    end sub

    function Position(videoId as string) as integer
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.videoId = videoId then return entry.position
        end for
        return 0
    end function

    function IsWatching(videoId as string) as boolean
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.videoId = videoId then return true
        end for
        return false
    end function

    ' The continue-watching stack as-is: newest first, already capped.
    function ContinueWatching() as object
        return m.positions
    end function

    ' The most recent continue-watching entry for one series/movie, or invalid
    ' when nothing has been watched. Details uses this to resurrect a resume
    ' hint for episodes opened straight from a catalog row. Since the array is
    ' newest-first, the first match is the one to resume.
    function ResumeFor(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.metaId = metaId then return entry
        end for
        return invalid
    end function

    function RemovePosition(videoId as string) as boolean
        for i = m.positions.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            if m.positions[i].videoId = videoId
                m.positions.Delete(i)
                m.Save()
                return true
            end if
        end for
        return false
    end function

    ' ---- watched state ----

    ' Record that a video finished (position >= duration * WATCHED_THRESHOLD),
    ' when the player knows a duration. Coalesces like SetPosition: the key is
    ' the video id (a movie's metaId, or a series' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}")
    ' so re-watching never duplicates. The local set is display-side only — it
    ' is written here on both guest and stremio sessions but never pushed to the
    ' account (the push clones the account's own flags, see BuildWatchStateItem).
    sub MarkWatchedIfFinished(metaId as string, videoId as string, position as integer, duration as integer)
        if duration <= 0 then return
        if position < duration * WATCHED_THRESHOLD then return
        key = metaId
        if videoId <> "" then key = videoId
        if key = "" then return
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, key) then return
        m.watched[key] = true
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' Coarse whole-item watched: the local set has the metaId, or the account
    ' layer flagged the whole item watched (flaggedWatched/timesWatched). Movies
    ' answer directly; series tiles should use SeriesStatus for the watched/
    ' progress distinction.
    function IsWatched(metaId as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" then return false
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return true
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account <> invalid and account.watched then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' Per-episode watched, precise. Local set first; when the episode list is
    ' available the account bitfield is decoded against it (it is only an index
    ' into that ordering, so without the list the account part cannot answer).
    ' "orderedEpisodes" is the series' ordered video id list.
    function EpisodeWatched(metaId as string, season as integer, episode as integer, orderedEpisodes as object) as boolean
        if orderedEpisodes = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodes) <> "roArray" then return false
        videoId = metaId + ":" + season.ToStr() + ":" + episode.ToStr()
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, videoId) then return true
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return true
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account = invalid then return false
        if account.bitfield = "" then return false
        codec = WatchedCodec()
        watched = codec.WatchedDecode(account.bitfield, orderedEpisodes)
        if watched <> invalid and m.HasKey(watched, videoId) then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' Coarse series status for grid tiles that have no episode list. "done" when
    ' the whole series is known watched (local MarkSeriesDone, or the account
    ' flagged the series watched); "progress" when some watch state exists
    ' (account in-progress, or the account bitfield covers part of the list);
    ' "none" otherwise. Precise done (every episode) needs the episode list and
    ' is EpisodesScreen's job.
    function SeriesStatus(metaId as string) as string
        if metaId = "" then return "none"
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return "done"
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account = invalid then return "none"
        if account.watched then return "done"
        if account.inProgress or account.bitfield <> "" then return "progress"
        return "none"
    end function

    ' The existing continue-watching position for a meta, as the progress bar
    ' needs it (position/duration in ms), or invalid when there is none.
    function ProgressFor(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.metaId = metaId
                return { position: entry.position, duration: entry.duration }
            end if
        end for
        return invalid
    end function

    ' Persist a whole-series done flag (guest local, stremio display-only like
    ' the watched set). Used by EpisodesScreen once it has the full episode list
    ' and can see every non-special episode is watched.
    sub MarkSeriesDone(metaId as string)
        if metaId = "" then return
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return
        m.watched[metaId] = true
        m.Save()
    end sub

    function AccountLayer(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if m.HasKey(m.accountWatched, metaId) then return m.accountWatched[metaId]
        return invalid
    end function

    ' Reconcile the store with the account's remote library (from the
    ' datastoreGet pull). The API is the authority, so the whole in-memory state
    ' is rebuilt, never merged: continue watching is re-derived and re-ordered,
    ' the saved map is re-filled, and every item (even non-CW ones) is kept in
    ' stremioLibrary for the future Library screen. Only the continue-watching
    ' stack is written to the device (Save gates it); the rest lives for the
    ' session. Stremio sessions only — a guest store has no library to reconcile
    ' with, and a stray call must never clobber local guest data.
    sub SyncFromStremio(items as dynamic)
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return
        if items = invalid or Type(items) <> "roArray" then return

        m.stremioLibrary = items
        cw = []
        saved = {}
        savedOrder = []
        accountWatched = {}
        for each item in items
            parsed = m.ParseLibraryItem(item)
            if parsed = invalid then continue for
            ' The account layer: re-derived on every sync, memory-only. It peers
            ' into the item's watch state the same way the app's own watched set
            ' does — flaggedWatched/timesWatched mark a whole item watched,
            ' timeOffset marks it in progress, and the raw watched bitfield is
            ' kept whole so EpisodesScreen can decode it against the episode list.
            accountWatched[parsed.metaId] = {
                watched: parsed.watchedFlag
                inProgress: parsed.inProgress
                bitfield: parsed.bitfield
            }
            if parsed.cw then cw.Push(parsed)
            if parsed.saved and parsed.metaId <> "" and not m.HasKey(saved, parsed.metaId)
                saved[parsed.metaId] = {
                    metaId: parsed.metaId
                    metaType: parsed.metaType
                    name: parsed.name
                    poster: parsed.poster
                }
                savedOrder.Push(parsed.metaId)
            end if
        end for

        ' Continue watching, newest first. Exactly one resume point survives per
        ' distinct video OR series (mirroring SetPosition's prune), and the stack
        ' is capped at MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING. Tracking seen ids instead of
        ' deleting as we go is what keeps the NEWEST occurrence of each
        ' video/series — a delete-then-push pass over a newest-first array would
        ' leave only the oldest.
        m.SortByMtimeDesc(cw)
        positions = []
        seenVideo = {}
        seenMeta = {}
        for each entry in cw
            if not m.HasKey(seenMeta, entry.metaId) and not m.HasKey(seenVideo, entry.videoId)
                seenMeta[entry.metaId] = true
                seenVideo[entry.videoId] = true
                positions.Push({
                    videoId: entry.videoId
                    metaId: entry.metaId
                    metaType: entry.metaType
                    season: entry.season
                    episode: entry.episode
                    name: entry.name
                    poster: entry.poster
                    position: entry.position
                    duration: entry.duration
                })
            end if
        end for
        while positions.Count() > MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING
            positions.Pop()
        end while
        m.positions = positions

        m.saved = saved
        m.savedOrder = savedOrder
        m.accountWatched = accountWatched
        print "[rokumio] LibraryStore sync cw=" + m.positions.Count().ToStr() + " saved=" + m.savedOrder.Count().ToStr() + " total=" + m.stremioLibrary.Count().ToStr()
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' The full synced library, kept in memory for the future Library screen.
    function StremioLibraryItems() as object
        return m.stremioLibrary
    end function

    ' Classify one datastoreGet library item and pre-map it into the store's
    ' shape. An item that cannot be resolved to a video id (or is not a valid
    ' item at all) comes back invalid so it never becomes a continue-watching
    ' entry; it still lives in the raw stremioLibrary since that keeps everything
    ' the API returned.
    '
    ' Continue watching: timeOffset > 0 && type != "other" && (!removed || temp).
    ' Saved: removed == false && temp == false. Position/duration are the raw ms
    ' values — the player tracks time in milliseconds too, so no conversion.
    '
    ' The account watched layer rides on the same item's state: flaggedWatched
    ' (an explicit "mark all watched" toggle) or timesWatched means the whole
    ' item is watched on the account; timeOffset > 0 means it is in progress;
    ' the raw state.watched bitfield (if any) is kept whole for precise per-
    ' episode decoding on EpisodesScreen. None of it is recalculated here — it
    ' is read off the server exactly as Stremio stores it.
    function ParseLibraryItem(item as dynamic) as dynamic
        if item = invalid or Type(item) <> "roAssociativeArray" then return invalid
        if item._id = invalid or item._id = "" then return invalid
        metaId = item._id
        metaType = item.type
        if metaType = invalid or metaType = "" then metaType = "movie"
        name = item.name
        if name = invalid then name = ""
        poster = item.poster
        if poster = invalid then poster = ""
        removed = item.removed = true
        temp = item.temp = true

        position = 0
        duration = 0
        videoId = metaId
        watchedFlag = false
        bitfield = ""
        state = item.state
        if state <> invalid and Type(state) = "roAssociativeArray"
            if state.timeOffset <> invalid then position = state.timeOffset
            if state.duration <> invalid then duration = state.duration
            if state.video_id <> invalid and state.video_id <> "" then videoId = state.video_id
            if state.flaggedWatched <> invalid and state.flaggedWatched > 0 then watchedFlag = true
            if state.timesWatched <> invalid and state.timesWatched > 0 then watchedFlag = true
            if state.watched <> invalid and (Type(state.watched) = "roString" or Type(state.watched) = "String") then bitfield = state.watched
        end if
        inProgress = position > 0

        season = 0
        episode = 0
        parts = videoId.Split(":")
        if parts.Count() = 3
            season = parts[1].ToInt()
            episode = parts[2].ToInt()
        else if parts.Count() <> 1
            return invalid
        end if

        mtime = item._mtime
        if mtime = invalid then mtime = ""
        return {
            cw: position > 0 and metaType <> "other" and (not removed or temp)
            saved: not removed and not temp
            metaId: metaId
            metaType: metaType
            name: name
            poster: poster
            videoId: videoId
            season: season
            episode: episode
            position: position
            duration: duration
            mtime: mtime
            watchedFlag: watchedFlag
            inProgress: inProgress
            bitfield: bitfield
        }
    end function

    ' Newest first by _mtime (ISO timestamps sort lexicographically). An
    ' insertion sort keeps it interpreter-safe; roArray.Sort's function
    ' comparator is not guaranteed in the brs interpreter.
    sub SortByMtimeDesc(entries as object)
        for i = 1 to entries.Count() - 1
            temp = entries[i]
            j = i
            while j > 0 and entries[j - 1].mtime < temp.mtime
                entries[j] = entries[j - 1]
                j = j - 1
            end while
            entries[j] = temp
        end for
    end sub

    ' Build the full LibraryItem a datastorePut push sends after a position
    ' update. The account is the source of truth for fields this app does not
    ' author, so the push clones the freshest cached copy of the item (from the
    ' last sync) and overwrites only the watch-state fields the player knows —
    ' video_id, timeOffset, duration, lastWatched — plus _mtime. Server-authored
    ' fields (timesWatched, the watched bitfield, flaggedWatched, behaviorHints,
    ' the removed/temp flags) survive untouched; SyncFromStremio reads them into
    ' the account watched layer (m.accountWatched) at pull time, and they go back
    ' unchanged on push so this app never overwrites what the account knows. An
    ' item the cache has never seen (added on another device between sync and
    ' push) falls back to a minimal temp entry so the server records the progress
    ' without promoting it to the permanent library. Guest sessions never write
    ' back, so the call is refused there too (mirrors SyncFromStremio). `now` is
    ' injectable for tests; production lets it default and NowIso() stamps it.
    function BuildWatchStateItem(packet as dynamic, now = "" as string) as dynamic
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return invalid
        if packet = invalid then return invalid
        metaId = packet.metaId
        if metaId = invalid or metaId = "" then return invalid
        videoId = packet.videoId
        if videoId = invalid or videoId = "" then videoId = metaId
        position = 0
        if packet.position <> invalid then position = packet.position
        duration = 0
        if packet.duration <> invalid then duration = packet.duration
        metaType = packet.metaType
        if metaType = invalid or metaType = "" then metaType = "movie"
        name = ""
        if packet.name <> invalid then name = packet.name
        poster = ""
        if packet.poster <> invalid then poster = packet.poster
        if now = "" then now = m.NowIso()

        original = invalid
        for each item in m.stremioLibrary
            if item <> invalid and item._id = metaId then original = item : exit for
        end for
        if original = invalid
            return {
                _id: metaId
                name: name
                type: metaType
                poster: poster
                removed: true
                temp: true
                _mtime: now
                state: {
                    lastWatched: now
                    timeOffset: position
                    duration: duration
                    video_id: videoId
                }
            }
        end if

        clone = {}
        for each key in original
            clone[key] = original[key]
        end for
        state = {}
        oldState = original.state
        if oldState <> invalid and Type(oldState) = "roAssociativeArray"
            for each key in oldState
                state[key] = oldState[key]
            end for
        end if
        state.video_id = videoId
        state.timeOffset = position
        state.duration = duration
        state.lastWatched = now
        clone.state = state
        clone._mtime = now
        return clone
    end function

    ' Build the full LibraryItem a datastorePut push sends after an add/remove
    ' toggle. Mirrors BuildWatchStateItem: a stremio-only, cache-read-only
    ' builder. The push clones the freshest cached copy of the item (from the
    ' last sync) so untracked server fields survive, or falls back to a minimal
    ' record when the cache has never seen the title (toggled before the first
    ' sync landed). The membership flags are the whole story: an add is
    ' removed:false/temp:false, a remove is removed:true/temp:false — the id
    ' stays in the account library marked removed, so re-adding later is the
    ' same item with removed:false. `now` is injectable for tests; production
    ' lets it default and NowIso() stamps it. The cache is never mutated — the
    ' next datastoreGet replaces it wholesale.
    function BuildLibraryChangeItem(metaId as string, metaType as string, name as string, poster as string, added as boolean, now = "" as string) as dynamic
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return invalid
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        if metaType = invalid or metaType = "" then metaType = "movie"
        if name = invalid then name = ""
        if poster = invalid then poster = ""
        if now = "" then now = m.NowIso()

        original = invalid
        for each item in m.stremioLibrary
            if item <> invalid and item._id = metaId then original = item : exit for
        end for
        if original = invalid
            return {
                _id: metaId
                name: name
                type: metaType
                poster: poster
                removed: not added
                temp: false
                _mtime: now
            }
        end if

        clone = {}
        for each key in original
            clone[key] = original[key]
        end for
        clone.removed = not added
        clone.temp = false
        clone._mtime = now
        return clone
    end function

    ' ISO-8601 UTC timestamp for _mtime/lastWatched, via roDateTime.ToISOString
    ' (no manual month/day assembly, so no 0-indexed month gotcha). Returns ""
    ' when the platform cannot produce one.
    function NowIso() as string
        try
            dt = CreateObject("roDateTime")
            if dt = invalid then return ""
            iso = dt.ToISOString()
            if iso = invalid then return ""
            return iso
        catch e
            return ""
        end try
    end function

    ' The player publishes each position update as a watch-state packet here
    ' (memory-only) as well as through its own field, so MainScene can still read
    ' the last packet after the player node is torn down — its async field
    ' observer races the pop that releases the component (and the video node it
    ' holds). Reading from the store has no node-lifetime dependency.
    '
    ' Note: the getter is LatestWatchStatePacket, NOT LatestWatchState —
    ' BrightScript member names are case-insensitive, so a method named
    ' LatestWatchState would collide with the m.latestWatchState field it reads
    ' (a runtime crash, same class of bug as the StremioLibrary() rename).
    sub RecordWatchState(packet as dynamic)
        if packet = invalid then return
        m.latestWatchState = packet
    end sub

    function LatestWatchStatePacket() as dynamic
        return m.latestWatchState
    end function

    ' Guest/stremio sessions persist under different keys so one session can
    ' never surface the other's saved content or continue-watching positions.
    function RegistryKey() as string
        if m.sessionType = "stremio" then return "stremio_library"
        return "library"
    end function

    ' Repoint the store at another session's data. A same-session switch is a
    ' no-op; everything is reloaded fresh so the in-memory state always mirrors
    ' the active session's persisted key.
    sub SwitchSession(sessionType as string)
        if sessionType <> "guest" and sessionType <> "stremio" then return
        if m.sessionType = sessionType then return
        m.sessionType = sessionType
        m.saved = {}
        m.savedOrder = []
        m.positions = []
        m.watched = {}
        m.accountWatched = {}
        m.Load()
    end sub

    sub Save()
        if m.registry = invalid then return
        data = { continueWatching: m.positions }
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            data.saved = m.saved
            data.savedOrder = m.savedOrder
            data.watched = m.watched
        end if
        m.registry.Write(m.RegistryKey(), FormatJson(data))
        m.registry.Flush()
    end sub

    sub Load()
        if m.registry = invalid then return
        raw = m.registry.Read(m.RegistryKey())
        if raw = "" then return
        parsed = invalid
        try
            parsed = ParseJson(raw)
        catch e
            return
        end try
        if parsed = invalid then return
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            if parsed.saved <> invalid and Type(parsed.saved) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.saved = parsed.saved
            if parsed.savedOrder <> invalid and Type(parsed.savedOrder) = "roArray" then m.savedOrder = parsed.savedOrder
            if parsed.watched <> invalid and Type(parsed.watched) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.watched = parsed.watched
        end if
        if parsed.continueWatching <> invalid and Type(parsed.continueWatching) = "roArray" then m.positions = parsed.continueWatching
    end sub
end class
